hi i'm merle i am a tasty producer in  new york and today i'm going to tell you  why i started tasty veg  okay so this first video was one of the  ones that i was experimenting with when  i first started doing vegetarian content  this one was tricky but once you get the  hang of the cutting motion it's super  super simple my approach to this was to  just pick one vegetable at a time and  then see how many different ways i could  cook it or bake it and i was focusing on  potatoes and i found out that this is  actually a really popular street food  all over the world so i think that lent  itself to the success of the video a lot  of people be like i've seen this in my  city or i've seen this in japan or i've  seen this in mexico  this video is different because you  wouldn't look at this and be like oh  that's a vegetarian video you would just  be like oh that's so cool i want to try  that i bet you i could do that since it  did so well it caught my boss's  attention and he was like wow maybe it  is actually possible for you to do  plant-based food and it can go viral  after the success of the tornado potato  and a handful of other vegetarian videos  i made for tasty i was allowed to start  the tasty vegetarian page just kind of  as an experiment to see how vegetarian  content can work and if our audience was  large enough to handle its own page of  just that content so about a month into  starting the tasty vegetarian page i had  the idea to make a video about how you  could regrow your own fruits at home the  idea behind this was that you could save  money i was pretty sure a lot of people  didn't even know you could regrow your  own food and it seemed like a good use  for kitchen scraps so i dove into this  project and it ended up paying off  tenfold it's by far my most successful  video probably the one i've put the most  love into i was still relatively new as  a producer when i made this video but i  just dove into this project because i  was so excited about it so i had the  whole thing shot three weeks into all my  hard work and then i submitted it for  notes and i got the feedback that i  should have gone through research first  because we needed to make sure the stuff  i was putting out to the world was  actually true so  i ended up having to wait an additional  two and a half weeks before we could  actually publish this video i think one  reason you'd want to regrow your own  fruit is because you more than likely  have at least one of these things in  your house as it is and you're gonna  throw the scraps away anyway so why not  make the scraps work for you and you  might be able to save a little bit of  money down the road i mean if you buy  something at a store and then you find  out that by buying that it can then make  another one for free it just sounds like  a genius idea to me not to mention you  actually know where your food is coming  from so there's the benefit of your  confidence in how healthy this actually  is for you and where your food is coming  from and whether or not you've used  pesticides the other really cool thing  and another reason you might want to try  regrowing your own fruit is that you can  do it pretty much in any sized apartment  or house in anywhere in the world so  there's no reason not to try it you'll  save money and it's fun so after this  video was published i was looking  through the comments and i saw all these  people telling me like there's no way  this works i'm sure you guys are faking  this but meanwhile i'd spent three weeks  running to flower shops and trying to  make this video happen  and then i have people like alvin at  work saying why would you even do this  it's not even a tasty video but then the  video blew up and i saw people  commenting pictures of their own regrown  gardens and all these positive comments  and it ended up being completely worth  it it's my favorite video  so you gotta work for the things you  love  well this pancake video was part of a  challenge we did to make a week of vegan  content through that week i actually  started to get interested in veganism  myself one of my goals is to make food  that's good first and vegan second and  these pancakes accomplish that in going  vegan i don't want to feel like i can't  eat the things i love and pancakes were  my favorite breakfast growing up and  they still are and so i just wanted to  make vegan pancakes that were just as  delicious fluffiness is important for  them to be delicious my goal with  veganism and my goal with making vegan  content is to just show people that it  doesn't have to be scary it doesn't have  to be bland and it doesn't have to be  hard but i will say i don't think you  need to be 100 vegan i think baby steps  and like you know don't feel guilty  about wanting to eat cheese cheese is  delicious just do any little bit that  you can i don't want anyone saying that  you're a horrible person just because  you're not vegan i want to show you a  vegan recipe that you don't want to pass  up on and then maybe from there on  forward you'll elect to eat vegan food  just because you want to doesn't have to  be every meal it could be one meal a  week one meal a month it could be one  meal a year i just think it's important  to try new things  one way that i come up with videos for  tasty vegetarian is that i'll look back  at what we've done in the past and see  what's done really well and then i'll  try to make a vegetarian version of that  so back in the day alvin made this one  pot swedish meatballs video that  absolutely killed i have to give it to  him and i was like okay alvin i'm gonna  make that dish but i'm gonna make it  vegan and it's gonna be just as  delicious something that i hope can  change  is that people will stop judging other  people for what they eat in the  decisions that they make about their  diet and instead start asking questions  and realize we're all doing our best  just because it's different doesn't mean  it's bad i was very happy with how these  swedish meatballs turned out if you're  gonna ask me if they tasted exactly like  meatballs like real meatballs with meat  of course not because they're not meat  however i can tell you they capture a  lot of the same savory notes and if  you're nostalgic for them and you miss  them and you don't eat meat they will  absolutely do the trick  the vegan cinnamon rolls were another  video that i made during our vegan week  sprint and the ideation was the same for  these i wanted to take a past hit video  from tasty and make it vegan two and a  half years ago i was hired at buzzfeed i  started as an intern as many of us do  and i was actually making food  pretty much from day one i worked really  really really hard for six months and  finally i was given the opportunity to  come on to the tasty team before tasty  there was buzzfeed food and i was making  videos for them but then tasty came  about and was a huge success and i was  lucky enough to jump on the team  buzzfeed is my first job it's the only  full-time job i've ever had and before i  came here i took a year and a half off  to go home and kind of figure out what i  wanted to do when i got to new york i  didn't have too much of a plan i just  applied to buzzfeed online and a day  after i moved to new york without any  real plan or any job i got a call saying  that they were interested in doing an  interview with me for an internship  position i was so excited i remember  calling my mom and my entire family and  kind of freaking out so six months after  i was hired as an intern i was offered a  full-time position with tasty and i was  a tasty producer i gladly accepted and  then basically turned around and said  okay well now i'm gonna be vegetarian  and i don't want to use any meat in any  of my videos i was really nervous at  first and wasn't sure how they were  going to take that but to my surprise  they were very open and they were very  accepting of my choice they were up for  the challenge they were like okay if you  can make vegetarian tasty videos work go  for it and i did this whole experience  has been incredibly humbling but also  it's given me the opportunity to really  trust my instinct and to believe that  other people will feel the same way that  i do and to see it as a success has  meant more to me than you can even  imagine i feel really good about what i  do and i'm lucky enough to enjoy going  to work every day and feel like i'm  doing a little bit of good for the world  because i've had the opportunity to take  something that i'm super passionate  about and make it approachable and easy  for people all over the world so i  really don't know anyone with a cooler  job than mine oh yes  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

